  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}})}{(3-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}},\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}$ and $\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}})}{(3-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & \\to \\frac{0-0}{3-0+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113169/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f75252e-bf7d-59ed-bb16-6a2b65a97863"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113169"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" :answer/id #uuid "ea820507-e4a6-550e-80b5-4ae6cde10644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "525be846-766c-5b21-9429-2c30da1a92ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" :answer/id #uuid "f1edc508-eac2-5d96-b5f5-647e52f9f349" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173/selection/653da0a030c613b91b907bdd7f4c3ddb1184ab9c4042623dec3f04f1600f942f" :answer/id #uuid "aa9faeb4-78a2-5681-9eb0-bf6ae3d7e636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173/selection/2594cd49a3336d3047d8064c75c37e35fc9daf64a171706cef41c80cbc6005d9" :answer/id #uuid "c8bb9674-11b4-5ee4-852b-d4ad672aa4a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d10d0f32-219d-5f98-a5f3-4582f493a66b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113173/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-113173/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" "q-113173/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-113173/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" "q-113173/selection/653da0a030c613b91b907bdd7f4c3ddb1184ab9c4042623dec3f04f1600f942f" "q-113173/selection/2594cd49a3336d3047d8064c75c37e35fc9daf64a171706cef41c80cbc6005d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113173" :question/id #uuid "b21ee535-539b-5078-9c48-3b1c819d693a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113173" :question/problem "Determine the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{7x+3}{6{x}^{7}-2{x}^{2}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{7}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{7},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{7x+3}{6{x}^{7}-2{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7x}{{x}^{7}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}})}{(\\frac{6{x}^{7}}{{x}^{7}}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{{x}^{6}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}})}{(6-\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{7}{{x}^{6}},\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}},\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{{x}^{6}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}})}{(6-\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}})} \\\\  & \\to \\frac{0+0}{6-0-0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113173/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f75252e-bf7d-59ed-bb16-6a2b65a97863"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113173"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "4dab9c13-38a6-55de-981e-ff634b08035d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" :answer/id #uuid "17bbe0a2-f33b-55d4-abe8-f5d3880e79a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176/selection/f7031104f14fe004994e4fe4b8af3fbe4e65cfa2bff3c7eab1748f5f2092c758" :answer/id #uuid "484feb8e-ebc4-5f36-a0a8-cb3ab1b50c99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176/selection/f5d98a631ee48ed70accf24f8b6cebcd32363395da4e87feeaf883d85b9bc131" :answer/id #uuid "aa2429b2-2299-5938-8580-2980ac815d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176/selection/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer/id #uuid "3fb24a27-f25c-5c92-a2b4-85eba6f7ee8b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "de09a269-0bd3-5614-a91c-ea5aa354b65b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113176/selection/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer-field/choices ["q-113176/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-113176/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" "q-113176/selection/f7031104f14fe004994e4fe4b8af3fbe4e65cfa2bff3c7eab1748f5f2092c758" "q-113176/selection/f5d98a631ee48ed70accf24f8b6cebcd32363395da4e87feeaf883d85b9bc131" "q-113176/selection/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113176" :question/id #uuid "6076d1df-0a51-5be4-8eb1-e4f9aaadd8b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113176" :question/problem "Determine the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{8}-4{x}^{4}+2x}{{x}^{6}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{6}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{8}-4{x}^{4}+2x}{{x}^{6}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{{x}^{6}}-\\frac{4{x}^{4}}{{x}^{6}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{6}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{{x}^{6}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}},$ $\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{{x}^{2}-0+0}{1-0} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-113176/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "653503b2-4631-561e-af5e-847bcbdfe8e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113176"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" :answer/id #uuid "df074941-0dd3-5341-afb9-6108b2add7c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" :answer/id #uuid "c11caacb-9c94-5c2f-8330-afdecfd4f3b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183/selection/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer/id #uuid "e07d0efd-4392-5fbe-8773-138a80e79e38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183/selection/ab35b5d31934a29f264b13e06671189d17ea95205c6933037fe20d8b552aa57e" :answer/id #uuid "654adcc5-319f-5657-bbd7-402ad3f4a0d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183/selection/2594cd49a3336d3047d8064c75c37e35fc9daf64a171706cef41c80cbc6005d9" :answer/id #uuid "77e3c3ca-6091-534d-807a-ef63a7afd5bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "48303d7a-e3f6-5cf4-a829-19a687ee1171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113183/selection/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer-field/choices ["q-113183/selection/763a7c0b26f15df25c2db2d8ac42125e806c2e4b56e4f070b4566eba7e05dfff" "q-113183/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" "q-113183/selection/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" "q-113183/selection/ab35b5d31934a29f264b13e06671189d17ea95205c6933037fe20d8b552aa57e" "q-113183/selection/2594cd49a3336d3047d8064c75c37e35fc9daf64a171706cef41c80cbc6005d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113183" :question/id #uuid "46cdbc89-38e8-5e50-824f-ae7d2846257a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113183" :question/problem "Determine the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{8{x}^{6}+3{x}^{2}-7}{{x}^{4}-6x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{4}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{4},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{8{x}^{6}+3{x}^{2}-7}{{x}^{4}-6x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8{x}^{6}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{6x}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(8{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}})}{(1-\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}},$ $\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}}$ and $\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(8{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}})}{(1-\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{8{x}^{2}+0-0}{1-0} \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-113183/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "653503b2-4631-561e-af5e-847bcbdfe8e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113183"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
